  {
    "title": "Introduction to Machine Learning",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "content": "Machine Learning: Transforming Data into Intelligence"
      },
      {
        "type": "diagram",
        "content": "graph TD
          A[Artificial Intelligence] --> B[Machine Learning]
          B --> C[Supervised Learning]
          B --> D[Unsupervised Learning]
          B --> E[Reinforcement Learning]"
      },
      {
        "type": "quote",
        "content": "Machine Learning: Teaching computers to learn from experience without being explicitly programmed"
      }
    ],
    "speakerNotes": "Introduce machine learning as a powerful approach to creating intelligent systems that can learn and improve from data.",
    "layout": "two-column",
    "outlineNodeId": "node_1"
  },
  {
    "title": "What is Machine Learning?",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "content": "Defining Machine Learning"
      },
      {
        "type": "bullet-points",
        "content": [
          "A subset of artificial intelligence",
          "Systems that improve through experience",
          "Learn patterns from data automatically",
          "Adapt and make intelligent decisions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "diagram",
        "content": "flowchart LR
          A[Raw Data] --> B[Machine Learning Algorithm]
          B --> C[Learned Patterns]
          C --> D[Intelligent Predictions]"
      }
    ],
    "speakerNotes": "Explain how machine learning differs from traditional programming by focusing on learning from data patterns.",
    "layout": "two-column",
    "outlineNodeId": "node_1_1"
  },
  {
    "title": "Types of Machine Learning",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "content": "Three Primary Learning Paradigms"
      },
      {
        "type": "diagram",
        "content": "flowchart TD
          A[Machine Learning Types] --> B[Supervised Learning]
          A --> C[Unsupervised Learning]
          A --> D[Reinforcement Learning]

          B --> B1[Labeled Training Data]
          B --> B2[Predictive Modeling]

          C --> C1[Unlabeled Data]
          C --> C2[Pattern Discovery]

          D --> D1[Learn through Interaction]
          D --> D2[Reward-based Learning]"
      },
      {
        "type": "bullet-points",
        "content": [
          "Supervised Learning: Predictive modeling with labeled data",
          "Unsupervised Learning: Discovering hidden patterns",
          "Reinforcement Learning: Learning through interaction and feedback"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "speakerNotes": "Break down the three main types of machine learning, highlighting their unique characteristics and use cases.",
    "layout": "diagram",
    "outlineNodeId": "node_1_1_1"
  }
]
